      "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept.\nAsset type: a game environment MODELLING TURNAROUND SHEET, not a landscape illustration.\nReference image 1: the user's ORIGINAL digital workshop island. Extract its warm sculpted limestone terrain craftsmanship, large fractured mineral volumes, honey-coloured earth and irregular tropical vegetation margins. The wooden workshop and props will be built separately.\nReference image 2: the original whole-archipelago reference, for the natural inhabited coastal geography and polished cartoon game art.\n\nCreate ONE rigorously coherent three-view modelling sheet of the SAME bare Projects island, on clean white, isolated and uncropped. This is a technical orthographic model sheet like a vehicle front/side/top drawing, NOT three aerial concept illustrations. Every terrain landmark has exactly the same position and shape in all three panels.\n\nLAYOUT:\nUpper-left: TRUE TOP PLAN, optical axis vertical. Rear/north at top, front/south at bottom, east at right. No vertical cliff faces visible in this panel.\nLower-left directly aligned under top: TRUE FRONT ELEVATION, optical axis horizontal with ZERO downward pitch, parallel projection. It shares exactly the top panel's X extents. Flat ground surfaces are edge-on, not wide visible lawns.\nLower-right: TRUE RIGHT ELEVATION, optical axis horizontal with ZERO downward pitch, parallel projection. Front/south at left, rear/north at right. No wide visible top clearing.\nUse consistent metric scale; front and right share a horizontal sea datum. Only small panel captions \"TOP\", \"FRONT\", \"RIGHT\" outside each object, no decorative UI. Blank upper-right space is acceptable. Crisp large detailed surfaces, high-resolution professional modeller reference sheet.\n\nSUBJECT — FOLLOW THE ORIGINAL WORKSHOP TERRAIN, NOT A NEW THREE-MESA ISLAND:\nOne connected, asymmetrical, terraced limestone mass, about60m wide by56m deep. A central wide IRREGULAR HONEY-EARTH workshop apron32x26m is genuinely horizontal at4.8m above implied sea level. It is not a domed hill or a green lawn. Around it are these SAME seven landmarks across views:\n1) An elongated honey-earth apron with small mineral outcrops and generous future building/walking space.\n2) ONE offset rear cannon ridge: broad upper terrace integrated with two staggered rock shoulders, not a free-standing central mountain or cylinder.\n3) A substantial front-left inclined limestone buttress with a deep vertical blue-grey cleft and worn rounded corners.\n4) An articulated front face: two or three broad interlocking stone spurs separated by deep recesses and a few small ledges. Uneven non-circular silhouette, not an unbroken retaining wall.\n5) A narrower lower front-right headland with a legible future approach to the east bridge, no actual bridge yet.\n6) A smaller rear-right saddle linked continuously to the cannon ridge by a soil/stone terrace, not a third isolated monolith.\n7) A distinctive small right-flank rock incision below the cannon zone, reserved for a future waterfall; terrain channel only, no water/effect.\nMaintain a low sea-relative inhabited level and natural sandy descent at two coastal pockets; the tall original reference cliffs are adapted downward, not turned into a floating plateau.\nRock covers steep escarpments/spurs/clefts, compact honey earth covers the central apron and connections; olive-green grass/moss is in interrupted pockets on ledges/rims/cracks, no continuous grass cap. Sand is limited to low coves, NOT an even beige ring.\nLarge sculpted interlocking limestone planes with oblique fractures, chamfered weathered corners and selected dark grey-blue clefts, visibly different stratum widths. Detailed enough to reproduce with actual rock geometry; not small random noise on primitives.\nThe submerged solid body continues broadly10m below a subtle common sea datum in FRONT/RIGHT, never an exposed taper/cone or hanging rock stem. Exact TOP must hide submerged sides.\n\nSTYLE:\nPremium polished tropical cartoon game environment, smooth non-pixelated material detail and credible volume, original art. Neutral soft studio light with readable geology, not dramatic baked light/shadow. The shape/material craftsmanship must match the user's image, not a simple low-poly game blockout.\n\nEXCLUDE:\nNo buildings, timber decks, bridges, palms, trees, shrubs, flowers, waterfalls, boats, people, cannons, signs, lamps, sky, ocean plane or other islands; these will be separate elements. No isometric/three-quarter tilt, no aerial elevations, no smooth green blob, round disc, disconnected stacked pillars, voxel/pixel style, plastic clay toy, thin terrain card, copied labels from reference, logos or watermark."
    }
